## Jev's perfect week turns a two-man race into an all-out sprint to the finish.
For all the concern surrounding Oregon's playoff hopes, the Ducks did exactly what they needed to do against Michigan.

Win.

And win convincingly.

Oregon controlled the game from start to finish, taking care of business against the Wolverines and avoiding the kind of late-season stumble that has claimed contenders across the country.

The reward?

The Ducks currently sit #13 in the College Football Playoff rankings, close enough to keep the dream alive, but still on the outside looking in.

That's the good news.

The bad news is that style points probably matter from here on out.

Oregon can't afford many quiet wins. The Ducks need to keep stacking victories while hoping a few teams above them decide to trip over their own shoelaces.

Fortunately, there won't be much time to celebrate.

Michigan State comes to town Friday night, giving Oregon another opportunity to make a statement and continue building a playoff resume.

November football is stressful enough. Friday night football somehow finds a way to make it even worse.

